1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,202
This video shows the Columns Requirements table of a content import:

2
00:00:05,202 --> 00:00:08,836
which columns a file can have for each part and field of a

3
00:00:08,836 --> 00:00:13,890
content type, what each value looks like, and how to update items you already have.

4
00:00:18,490 --> 00:00:20,528
An import file is a table.

5
00:00:20,528 --> 00:00:25,112
Its first row names the columns, and each column feeds one part or

6
00:00:25,112 --> 00:00:27,150
field of the content type.

7
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:32,762
Every content type has its own columns, because its parts and fields are its own.

8
00:00:32,762 --> 00:00:36,730
The import page lists exactly the columns of the type you picked.

9
00:00:37,480 --> 00:00:40,523
Read the table, and you know the file you need.

10
00:00:40,523 --> 00:00:42,590
Anything not in it is ignored.

11
00:00:46,798 --> 00:00:51,373
On the import page for a type, the upload requirements come first.

12
00:00:51,373 --> 00:00:55,758
Download template gives a file with every column already named.

13
00:00:55,758 --> 00:00:58,490
The ContentItemId column is optional.

14
00:00:58,490 --> 00:01:02,430
Leave it empty to create an item, or fill it in with the

15
00:01:02,430 --> 00:01:05,544
id of an existing item to update that item.

16
00:01:05,544 --> 00:01:08,658
The title is the only required column here.

17
00:01:09,109 --> 00:01:10,640
Parts come first.

18
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:14,369
The HTML body and the Markdown body take the text.

19
00:01:14,369 --> 00:01:18,164
The alias and the URL path take the item's address.

20
00:01:18,164 --> 00:01:22,825
The archive and publish dates schedule the item, and are in UTC.

21
00:01:22,825 --> 00:01:25,289
A Liquid part takes a template.

22
00:01:25,739 --> 00:01:30,492
Then the type's own fields, named after the part and the field.

23
00:01:30,492 --> 00:01:34,970
A text field takes text, and a number field takes a number.

24
00:01:34,970 --> 00:01:38,276
Date and time fields take dates and times.

25
00:01:38,276 --> 00:01:41,169
A boolean field takes True or False.

26
00:01:41,620 --> 00:01:47,169
A multiple text field takes all its values in one cell, separated by a bar.

27
00:01:47,169 --> 00:01:50,594
A link has its URL, its text and its target.

28
00:01:50,594 --> 00:01:53,197
A YouTube field has its address.

29
00:01:53,197 --> 00:01:58,540
A content picker takes the ids of the items to link, separated by a bar.

30
00:02:02,741 --> 00:02:06,423
Here is a file with two events, using those columns:

31
00:02:06,423 --> 00:02:11,185
the title, the alias and path, the location, the number of seats, the

32
00:02:11,185 --> 00:02:16,201
dates and times, whether the event is featured, the speakers, and a link.

33
00:02:16,652 --> 00:02:19,113
Choose the file and click Upload.

34
00:02:19,113 --> 00:02:24,982
The import runs in the background, and the Import and Export page follows its progress.

35
00:02:27,576 --> 00:02:32,145
When it has finished, the events are content items like any other, with

36
00:02:32,145 --> 00:02:34,756
every field filled in from its column.

37
00:02:38,956 --> 00:02:43,489
Export the items of a type, and the file has the same columns,

38
00:02:43,489 --> 00:02:46,756
with ContentItemId filled in for every row.

39
00:02:47,506 --> 00:02:52,072
Change the values you want in a spreadsheet, and import the file.

40
00:02:52,072 --> 00:02:57,346
Each row with an id updates its item, and rows without one create new items.

41
00:02:58,096 --> 00:03:01,917
The table of a type is the contract in both directions, so a

42
00:03:01,917 --> 00:03:04,986
file you exported can always be imported again.

43
00:03:09,186 --> 00:03:12,086
Load a catalog of items from a spreadsheet.

44
00:03:12,836 --> 00:03:15,886
Fix a field on many items at once.

45
00:03:16,636 --> 00:03:19,876
Schedule items to publish later, in bulk.

46
00:03:20,626 --> 00:03:23,096
Move content between sites.

47
00:03:25,096 --> 00:03:27,959
Open the table, name the columns, and import.

48
00:03:27,959 --> 00:03:32,226
The user manual and the technical guide are linked in the description.

49
00:03:32,226 --> 00:03:33,686
Thanks for watching.

